  "_comment": "Level-up dons (the Stasis server's gameplay rules, rewritten for Jondo; Managers/Stasis/Dons.cs reads this). Every level gained from 2 to lastDonLevel offers cardsPerOffer cards (research quatrieme_carte adds one) and the player keeps one. Which offer a level gives, first rule that matches: passiveLevel -> the breed's class passives (all of them shown); spellLevels -> three spell dons of the class (spell_dons.json, SpellDons.cs), or when none is left the spell card, the characteristic card and level cards; a multiple of adventureEvery -> adventure dons; otherwise the characteristic card (with characteristicCard.firstChance) and level cards. accomplishmentLevels give an accomplishment offer, past lastDonLevel too. The normal characteristic points of a level are untouched: a don is on top. Stats are the French names Dons.StatIds knows (force, vitalite, puissance, dommagesFeu, resTerre, ...); 'decouverte' is a percent of experience, not a characteristic. Dofus 3 has no spell points (spells come with the level): the spell levels offer spell dons, and the spell card (Puissance) is only their fallback once every spell don is taken or capped. Movement speed is not something this server models, so the Stasis 'Vitesse' adventure don is left out. Adventure dons stack up to maxRank, their effects counted once per rank.",
